The target identifier is derived from libavformat/version.h/version_major.h.
It identifies the selected serialization compatibility profile,not an executing
FFmpeg library. Runtime processing remains TypeScript/independent Wasm.

The TypeScript adaptation uses finite packet/sample plans,bounded asynchronous
writes,cancellation,transaction aborts and explicitly selected low-level API
profiles. Low-level defaults retain their pre-profile behavior. General metadata,
all RIFF layouts and project-wide redistribution/attribution auditing remain open.

The reference-profile channel mask also follows the default-normal-compliance
write_channel_mask threshold in riffenc.c:mask>=0x40000 is serialized as0,
without altering the declared in-memory input layout. Other strictness modes
remain outside this scope.
